Package: stek-plugin-python
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         python3-cryptography (>= 42),
         lsb-cprocsp-capilite-64,
         lsb-cprocsp-kc1-64
Recommends: cprocsp-pki-cades-64,
            cprocsp-legacy-64
Suggests: cprocsp-rdr-pcsc-64,
          cprocsp-rdr-rutoken-64,
          ifd-rutokens
Description: Python reproduction of Стэк.Плагин (StekTrustPlugin) local HTTP service
 Protocol-compatible reimplementation of the StekTrustPlugin 2.7.0.9 local
 signing service (127.0.0.1:18080, /TRUST/). It exposes the same commands
 (PING, ENUMCERTS, GETSIGN, SIGN_HASH, DECRYPT, ...) to browser clients and
 delegates all cryptography to CryptoPro CSP.
 .
 No GOST/CMS/ASN.1/XML-DSig is implemented here: signing, decryption and hash
 signing go through CryptoPro's certified libraries, via the official pycades
 binding when available or the cryptcp/certmgr command-line tools otherwise.
 X.509 parsing uses python3-cryptography.
 .
 The CryptoPro packages are distributed by CryptoPro, not from the Debian
 archive; see /usr/share/doc/stek-plugin-python/README.Debian.
